From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Admin panel: Plans & Trials tab — the price list the website and app read
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New tab `/plans`, beside Shop Settings. It is the only place the partner price
list exists now: the website reads the public twin of this list, the app follows,
and a price change reaches both on their next load instead of needing a release of
either.

  · Free trial length, at the top, with the phrase it will render as
    ("3 Months (90 Days)") so what the partner reads is never a guess. Saving it
    updates the free row's `days`, which is what `salonLogin.js` computes a new
    salon's window from — the API and the portal cannot disagree again. The
    90-day default is in the seed; the screen simply shows what is stored.
  · One card per plan with, in place: name on the pricing screen, price (₹),
    length in days (derived phrase under it), sort order, optional ribbon, the
    one-line note, and a Recommended flag. Each card shows N active · M total
    salons, so the consequence of taking a plan off sale is visible before the
    click.
  · Save / Take off sale / Remove. Off sale keeps every salon already on it valid
    and renewable and hides it from the website's picker. Remove asks first and
    offers the right answer per plan — "Take off sale instead" when salons are on
    it, "Delete permanently" when none are — and the backend enforces the same
    rule, so a partner's subscription cannot be lost even from a bypassed client.
  · A banner lists salons sitting on a legacy plan id that has no row, with
    per-id counts, so their renewal never falls back to a 30-day default
    unnoticed. Nothing is renamed automatically.
  · Add a plan: name, price, length, note. The id is slugged from the name and
    never changes afterwards, because every paid subscription stores it.

Client-side validation mirrors the API: a name is required, a price cannot be
negative, a length must be 1–3650 days, and a paid plan cannot be priced at ₹0.
The tab is grantable in Role Management (it is in `TabArray`), and the super
admin — the role-management tab — sees it without granting it first, because
existing role rows were saved before this tab existed.
